WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.735
-Penn and --
-Hey, Jimmy, how you doing, man?

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.338
-I'm great. Thank you
so much for being here.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:08.040
You know, we always love it
when you guys come on the show.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.677
I personally love it.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.479
You know, I think
I've said this before.

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:15.281
You're one of the reasons
why I have a career,

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.617
is because of you guys,
and this goes back to the --

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:20.153
-And don't ever
forget that, Jimmy.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:23.389
-[ Laughs ]
Never! Never, never!

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:27.426
No, please, but it was
the Montreal Comedy Festival.

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:28.728
-Yes.
-Years ago.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.531
And I remember
it was new faces,

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:35.168
and I was brand-new, and I --
I had a manager and no agent.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:38.003
That's how --
Life is so weird at the time.

00:00:38.003 --> 00:00:40.940
And I go -- And she said, "Look,
when you get off the stage,

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.675
there's going to be
a lot of agents

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.177
that want to sign you,
so let me handle it."

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:47.547
Okay. I go, "Okay. Absolutely."
I was so nervous.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.549
I was ironing my shirt
and getting it all ready.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:52.151
I was probably 21.

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:54.787
And I got on stage,
and I had the worst act,

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.255
the worst performance
I ever had.

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:57.790
I just bombed. It was terrible.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.460
And I got off the stage,
and no one was waiting for me.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.763
And my manager was there,
and she was like --

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:06.899
She was trying to signal agents,
and no one wanted to see me.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:09.402
But the guys
that were running it,

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.270
Willie Mercer and Bruce Hills,

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.941
said, "Hey, we know
that your act is better,

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:17.376
and we showed it
to Penn &amp; Teller,

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.345
and so we asked them.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:22.081
Would you like to open for them
at the St-Denis Theatre

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.383
tomorrow night
at the Montreal --"

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:26.785
And I go, "Are you kidding me?"
I'd be honored."

00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:29.755
And I opened for you guys,
and I had a great night.

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:32.325
I crushed.
And I got off the stage.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.826
-You sure did. You were great.

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:35.160
-And there was my agent.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.630
I signed with APA at the time,
Danny Robinson,

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.132
and the rest is --

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:42.968
So I always mean to bring it up
and just say thanks again

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:45.171
'cause that meant so much to me
when I was first starting out.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.241
But I love you guys
and I love what you've done.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:53.079
And now you're in season 7
of "Fool Us," which I love,

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:57.783
but were you able to finish
filming before the quarantine?

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.719
-It was incredible.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:04.390
We wrapped on March 12th,
which was a Thursday.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.626
-Yeah, that was it.
-March 13th, the --

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:11.130
everybody finally was
finding out about the pandemic.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.833
And then Saturday, we were
supposed to have a live show

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:17.370
which we chose to not do
for the safety of our audiences,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.238
and then we've been
locked down ever since.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:21.807
So when you see "Fool Us,"

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:25.811
it's all this idyllic
pre-pandemic time.

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:28.114
-You came up with something fun
to show us tonight.

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:32.485
Have you -- Zoom magic.
Is this a --

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.354
I mean, you've been doing this
for 45 years.

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:37.156
Is this a curveball
that you didn't see coming?

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:40.259
-It's harder to do tricks
when the people can't touch

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:42.028
the props back and forth.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.762
But we've got something
that actually --

00:02:43.762 --> 00:02:46.132
We've got a card trick for you,
and when I say "we,"

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.600
I'm kind of wrong.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.869
Because Teller's
11 miles away from me.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.071
He's going to do the card trick
for you.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.973
And, Jimmy,
I'm just here to help

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.109
as kind of your guide
through this,

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.543
to make it a little better,

00:02:57.543 --> 00:02:59.412
but Teller's going to do
the trick for you.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.580
'Cause our problem is
we think card tricks

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.383
are often very, very wimpy.
-Yeah.

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:08.387
-So, we've got a trick
called the card stab.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.756
We're going to start
with you picking a card, Jimmy.

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:12.458
Teller will
riffle down the deck,

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:16.529
and you just have to yell "stop"
whenever you want.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.497
-Stop!
-Okay.

00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:20.432
That's the card
you chose right there.

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:23.002
The 3 -- Well, Teller --

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.937
The 3 of clubs is the card

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:27.106
we always use
when we're forcing a card.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.042
I have a 3 of clubs
ready all the time.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:32.078
That's kind of
our signature card.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:36.749
It's kind of an insult to Jimmy
to force a card on him

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.418
that we've forced on him before.

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.986
Get the card out of here.
I'm sorry, Jimmy.

00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:42.421
-No problem.
-Teller's --

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:44.556
You deserve more respect
than that.

00:03:44.556 --> 00:03:47.560
You'll have a real card
selected. Say stop again.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.395
-Sure. Stop.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:52.131
-Okay.
That's a legitimate card there.

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:54.600
The 4 of spades.
So remember that, Jimmy.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.802
That's important
for the card stab.

00:03:56.802 --> 00:03:58.837
And, now -- What --

00:03:58.837 --> 00:04:02.208
What the hell was that, Teller?
What the hell was that?

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:04.944
You put your shoulders up
like you were trying to fly.

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:07.980
I mean, even on Zoom,
that looked like a move.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.449 line:0%
Teller, show us the top card.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:12.618 line:0%
The top card of the deck.
Show it to us.

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:15.187
Yeah, he moved it
right to the top.

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:16.722
That was that move.

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:18.757
It was like he was trying
to teach somebody the move.

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:20.492
Give them a real shuffle,
Teller.

00:04:20.492 --> 00:04:22.761
Give them a real shuffle
and lose the card --

00:04:22.761 --> 00:04:24.664
Sorry, Jimmy.
We'll do this right.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.431
-No offense.
-And show us the top card.

00:04:26.431 --> 00:04:28.233
Show us the top card.

00:04:28.233 --> 00:04:30.035
Okay. That's not the card.

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:32.505
We're okay, Jimmy. That's fine.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.039
Teller --
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:37.176
What's -- What's
in your right hand, teller?

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:38.344
Show us your right hand.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.878
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:39.878 --> 00:04:42.381
-Yeah, he palmed off
the damn card.

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:44.417
And you've even got
your thumb sticking out,

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:47.353
so you're pointing to the idiot
that's palming a card.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:51.257
So put that back in the deck
and then shuffle them up.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.125
And you've got to
watch him, Jimmy.

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:56.328
Show us your hands empty.
Hands empty.

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:57.763
Not palmed there. Good. Okay.

00:04:57.763 --> 00:04:59.898
So, now the card's
really lost in the deck,

00:04:59.898 --> 00:05:02.135
and now he's really
putting them there.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.370
Now the trick starts, Jimmy.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.639
Now it's the card stab.
Go ahead, Teller.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.074
Do the --
Jimmy's not believing that!

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:10.809
You're looking down
by your nose.

00:05:10.809 --> 00:05:13.111
Just do the trick, Teller.

00:05:13.111 --> 00:05:15.247
Oh, you didn't even get a card.
You didn't even get a --

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:18.484
Teller, hurry up.
We're dying here.

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.153
Go. Go, go, go. Okay.
What are you --

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.221
That's not the card, Teller.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.623
He picked a black card.
That's a red card.

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:26.759
Just do it and do it fast!

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.027
Hurry, Teller, don't --

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:30.596
[ Teller screaming ]

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:35.968
-Is that your card, Jimmy?
The 4 of spades?

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.102
Is that your card right there?

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:39.505
-Yes. Teller, are you okay?!
What is go--

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.740
-There wasn't a knife there.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.643
It was just a --
It was just a gag.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.944
Jimmy's a little bit nervous

00:05:45.944 --> 00:05:48.114
about ripping your fingers off,
so be careful there.

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:51.083
Show them it's a trick there.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:53.219
There you go.
See, I just was here to help.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:55.521
I just helped.
-I love you guys so much.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:58.190
Teller, please stay safe.
Oh, my gosh.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.058
I love you guys.
Come back whenever.

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:02.327
And hopefully next time
we're in person. Okay?

00:06:02.327 --> 00:06:03.829
-Yeah, I hope so, too.

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:05.565
-Stay safe.
Penn &amp; Teller, everybody.

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:07.633
Check out
"Penn &amp; Teller: Fool Us"

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:10.269
Monday nights at 9:00 p.m.
on The CW.

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:12.872
More "Tonight Show"
after the break. Stick around.

